title: 'McClelland, McNaughton and O''Reilly (1995), complementary learning systems: a fast store keeps episodes apart, and a slow one learns from them by interleaved replay, so that new learning does not overwrite old.'
pid: 76982da9-6206-4fab-b264-561d41287447
body: |2-
  Summary, from reviews of it. The faulty-memory paper cites it for
  gating consolidation by fit with what is known. Took: two stores,
  raw and distilled, each kept; ours are Git and the transcripts beside
  the graph.
